.DS_Store

# Dev-only tooling, never imported by the deployed app (main.py/ask_service.py/
# providers.py don't reference anything under scripts/) — keep entirely out of
# the image, not just uninstalled. requirements-dev.txt pulls in Playwright,
# which needs a separate `playwright install chromium` plus Chromium's own
# system shared libraries (see scripts/chromium-deps.sh) neither of which this
# Dockerfile provides; excluding the file here means an accidental
# `pip install -r requirements-dev.txt` added to this Dockerfile later would
# fail loudly at build time (file not found) instead of silently trying, and
# failing at container runtime, to launch a browser that was never actually
# usable in this image.
requirements-dev.txt
scripts/
captures/

# p3m3 item #2.g -- local migration binaries, superseded by the Session 2
# Postgres migration (D2.5): chroma_store/ was the pre-migration vector
# store, now dead weight (all reads/writes go through operational_store.py's
# PgCollection); ingestion_quarantine/ holds the original source PDFs kept
# locally for provenance/recovery reference, not something the deployed app
# reads at runtime. Excluding both keeps the build context (and therefore
# the image) from carrying ~367MB neither COPY . . nor the app needs.
chroma_store/
ingestion_quarantine/
